# MediMate Rebranding: Backend Implementation Walkthrough

The MediMate frontend has been entirely refactored to align with the proposed "Backend" identity. Every interface element across the platform has been updated from the generic "health app" aesthetic to a stark, developer-focused aesthetic emphasizing structure, data flow, and precision.

## Changes Made

1. **Global Styles & Dashboard Themes**
    - Updated `styles.css`, `admin.css`, `caretaker.css`, and `dashboard.css`.
    - Integrated Ink Black backgrounds and absolute contrast colors across all CSS structure files.
    - Updated typography to reflect precise readouts: `Space Mono` for all headings/values and `DM Sans` for supporting body text.
    - Simplified geometry to structural grids, replacing all wide rounded padding/corners with hard-edged elements (0px–2px radius).

2. **Core Layout Updates**
    - Hand-edited the core interface files (`index.html`, `dashboard.html`, `admin.html`, and `caretaker.html`).
    - Swapped out consumer-friendly emojis (💊, 🌿, 🤖) for structural, data-oriented geometric glyphs (⬡, ◇, ▤, ⊞, ▯).
    - Rewrote all the user-facing text tags into system node terminology (e.g., "Patients" ⟶ "Target Nodes", "Messages" ⟶ "Comms Config", "Logout" ⟶ "Terminate Session").

